    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0110" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg48"/>

                <head>No. 37.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kasson to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 13, 1878</date>.
                        [Received July 30.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">97.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a copy of the original
                    text, with a translation, of the formal notification by the imperial government
                    of the acceptance by Austria and Hungary of the invitation extended to them on
                    the part of the United States to participate in the international conference on
                    the relations of gold and silver as money; an invitation communicated to this
                    government by me on the 8th of April last. This reply was to-day delivered to
                    this legation.</p>
                <p>There appears no objection to Paris as the place, or the 10th of August as the
                    time, for the meeting of the conference.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN A. KASSON.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d42-a1.xml" xpointer="d42-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
